{
  "name": "shortlists are staged privately, then confirmed irreversibly",
  "description": "RFC-0008 §3 and §3a. The consent flow is covered by contact_request_requires_consent; this case covers the two-phase model and the ownership rules around it.\n\nA shortlisted contributor can never be un-shortlisted — once someone has been told an organization is interested, that is a fact, and an endpoint that erased the record of it would be pretending otherwise. A rule that strict is only tolerable if there is a moment before it binds, so building a shortlist discloses NOTHING and only confirm sends anything.\n\nConfirm notifies exactly the entries where notified_at IS NULL. That makes the shortlist a living round: a fourth candidate on day 3 gets an email, and the original three are not re-notified. One rule for every entry whenever it was added — removable until confirmed, permanent after.\n\nScoping is to organization_id, so a departing recruiter does not take the hiring round with them. created_by and added_by are an audit trail, not an ownership claim.",
  "seed": ["principals", "catalogue", "repositories", "scored_population"],
  "steps": [
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists",
        "body": {
          "role_id": "{{acme.role}}",
          "name": "Platform team, Q3",
          "description": "Two Go/Kubernetes hires.",
          "tentative_result_date": "2026-09-15"
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "shortlist": "$.id"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "_note": "status is draft, not open. A shortlist that notified people the moment it was created is what the confirm step exists to prevent.",
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "role_id": "<uuid>",
          "name": "Platform team, Q3",
          "status": "draft",
          "tentative_result_date": "2026-09-15",
          "created_at": "<timestamp>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "tentative_result_date is required at creation. It is what the contributor is told, and the overdue ratio is computed against it — ADR-0005.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists",
        "body": {
          "role_id": "{{acme.role}}",
          "name": "Vague plans"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 422,
        "body": {
          "error": "invalid_shortlist",
          "items": [
            {
              "field": "tentative_result_date",
              "reason": "required"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists",
        "body": {
          "role_id": "{{acme.role}}",
          "name": "Backdated",
          "tentative_result_date": "2026-01-01"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 422,
        "_note": "A date already past would be born overdue and would immediately drag the org's flagging ratio.",
        "body": {
          "error": "invalid_shortlist",
          "items": [
            {
              "field": "tentative_result_date",
              "reason": "must_be_future"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "An unverified hirer cannot create one, even a draft that discloses nothing.",
      "as": "pending_pat",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists",
        "body": {
          "role_id": "{{unverified_org.role}}",
          "name": "Fishing",
          "tentative_result_date": "2026-09-15"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "error": "hiring_capability_required",
          "hirer_verified": false,
          "organization_verified": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "ORG SCOPING. dave_hiring is a different person at the same org and sees Hank's draft as their own.",
      "as": "dave_hiring",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/shortlists"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "total": 1,
          "shortlists": [
            {
              "id": "<uuid>",
              "role_id": "<uuid>",
              "name": "Platform team, Q3",
              "status": "draft",
              "tentative_result_date": "2026-09-15",
              "entry_count": 0,
              "unnotified_count": 0,
              "created_by": {
                "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
                "username": "hank",
                "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
                "active": true
              },
              "created_at": "<timestamp>"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A hirer at ANOTHER org sees nothing of Acme's, and cannot confirm an id they guessed.",
      "as": "sam_studio",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 404,
        "_note": "404 rather than 403 — a competitor must not be able to confirm that a given shortlist id belongs to Acme.",
        "body": {
          "error": "shortlist_not_found"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A colleague can edit it. The audit trail records Hank created it; it does not make it his.",
      "as": "dave_hiring",
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}",
        "body": {
          "name": "Platform team, Q3 (revised)",
          "tentative_result_date": "2026-09-30"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "name": "Platform team, Q3 (revised)",
          "description": "Two Go/Kubernetes hires.",
          "status": "draft",
          "tentative_result_date": "2026-09-30",
          "organization": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001",
            "name": "Acme Corp"
          },
          "created_by": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
            "username": "hank",
            "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
            "active": true
          },
          "entry_count": 0,
          "unnotified_count": 0,
          "first_confirmed_at": null,
          "updated_at": "<timestamp>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "AssertNotSelf fires at STAGE time, not at confirm — RFC-0008 §3a. Discovering an ineligible candidate at send time would be too late.",
      "as": "dave_hiring",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/entries",
        "body": {
          "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a004"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "error": "cannot_shortlist_self"
        },
        "db": {
          "shortlist_entries": {
            "where": {
              "shortlist_id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "count": 0
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Stage three candidates. NOTHING is disclosed by any of these.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/entries",
        "body": {
          "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001",
          "note": "Strongest Go evidence in the pool."
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "_note": "No contact_request field. There is no contact request — that is the entire point of the draft phase.",
        "body": {
          "shortlist_id": "<uuid>",
          "user": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001",
            "display_name": "Alice Okafor",
            "github_login": "aliceok"
          },
          "note": "Strongest Go evidence in the pool.",
          "added_by": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
            "username": "hank",
            "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
            "active": true
          },
          "notified_at": null,
          "added_at": "<timestamp>"
        },
        "db": {
          "shortlist_entries": {
            "where": {
              "shortlist_id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "count": 1,
            "all_match": {
              "notified_at": null
            }
          },
          "contact_requests": {
            "_note": "Zero. Staging is private.",
            "where": {
              "shortlist_id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "count": 0
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/entries",
        "body": {
          "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a002"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "body": {
          "shortlist_id": "<uuid>",
          "user": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a002",
            "display_name": "Bob Nakamura",
            "github_login": "bobn"
          },
          "note": null,
          "added_by": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
            "username": "hank",
            "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
            "active": true
          },
          "notified_at": null,
          "added_at": "<timestamp>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/entries",
        "body": {
          "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a003"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "_note": "Carol is INACTIVE — lapsed availability. She can still be staged and contacted; being quiet is not refusal (RFC-0008 §1a).",
        "body": {
          "shortlist_id": "<uuid>",
          "user": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a003",
            "display_name": "Carol Diaz",
            "github_login": "cdiaz"
          },
          "note": null,
          "added_by": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
            "username": "hank",
            "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
            "active": true
          },
          "notified_at": null,
          "added_at": "<timestamp>"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "THE MIS-CLICK REMEDY. Carol was staged by mistake and is removed. She was never told, so nothing is erased.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/entries/01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a003"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 204,
        "body": null,
        "db": {
          "shortlist_entries": {
            "where": {
              "shortlist_id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "count": 2
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "carol",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/contact-requests"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "Carol never learns she was briefly considered.",
        "body": {
          "total": 0,
          "requests": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A duplicate stage is a conflict. uq_contact_request is enforced at confirm, but a double entry is caught here.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/entries",
        "body": {
          "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 409,
        "body": {
          "error": "already_shortlisted"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "CONFIRM. Two emails, one transaction, and those two entries become permanent.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/confirm",
        "body": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "The response states the irreversibility in the payload, not only in the UI that led here.",
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "status": "open",
          "notified": 2,
          "already_notified": 0,
          "irreversible": true,
          "first_confirmed_at": "<timestamp>",
          "entries": [
            {
              "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001",
              "display_name": "Alice Okafor",
              "contact_request_id": "<uuid>",
              "notified_at": "<timestamp>"
            },
            {
              "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a002",
              "display_name": "Bob Nakamura",
              "contact_request_id": "<uuid>",
              "notified_at": "<timestamp>"
            }
          ]
        },
        "db": {
          "_note": "Every contact request for the round written atomically — the ADR-0005 same-transaction property, moved from add to confirm.",
          "contact_requests": {
            "where": {
              "shortlist_id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "count": 2,
            "all_match": {
              "status": "pending",
              "tentative_result_date": "2026-09-30"
            }
          },
          "shortlist_entries": {
            "where": {
              "shortlist_id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "count": 2,
            "none_match": {
              "notified_at": null
            }
          },
          "shortlists": {
            "where": {
              "id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "all_match": {
              "status": "open"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "ONCE SHORTLISTED, NEVER REMOVED. Alice was told; deleting the entry would erase the record of a disclosure that happened.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/entries/01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 409,
        "body": {
          "error": "entry_already_notified",
          "notified_at": "<timestamp>"
        },
        "db": {
          "shortlist_entries": {
            "where": {
              "shortlist_id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "count": 2
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "...and that holds before she answers, not only after. The disclosure, not the reply, is what binds.",
      "as": "alice",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/me/contact-requests"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "Acme is payment_verified, so no disclosure label. The sam_studio case pins the labelled variant.",
        "body": {
          "total": 1,
          "requests": [
            {
              "id": "<uuid>",
              "organization": {
                "name": "Acme Corp",
                "payment_verified": true,
                "verified": true
              },
              "status": "pending",
              "tentative_result_date": "2026-09-30",
              "disclosure": null,
              "role": {
                "id": "<uuid>",
                "title": "Backend engineer",
                "description": "Seeded so a round has a job to be for.",
                "engagement": "full_time",
                "location": "remote",
                "currency": "",
                "yearly_ctc": null,
                "yearly_base": null,
                "hourly_rate": null,
                "expected_hours": null,
                "eligible_countries": [],
                "requires_online_test": null,
                "max_interview_rounds": null,
                "avg_days_to_offer": null,
                "questions": []
              },
              "expires_at": "<timestamp>",
              "created_at": "<timestamp>"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A second confirm with nothing new sends nothing. Idempotent — a double click must not re-email anyone.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/confirm",
        "body": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "status": "open",
          "notified": 0,
          "already_notified": 2,
          "irreversible": true,
          "first_confirmed_at": "<timestamp>",
          "entries": []
        },
        "db": {
          "contact_requests": {
            "where": {
              "shortlist_id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "count": 2
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "DAY 3. A fourth candidate joins the same round rather than fragmenting it into a second shortlist.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/entries",
        "body": {
          "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a003"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "_note": "Staged, unnotified, and therefore removable again — even though the shortlist itself is already open.",
        "body": {
          "shortlist_id": "<uuid>",
          "user": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a003",
            "display_name": "Carol Diaz",
            "github_login": "cdiaz"
          },
          "note": null,
          "added_by": {
            "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
            "username": "hank",
            "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
            "active": true
          },
          "notified_at": null,
          "added_at": "<timestamp>"
        },
        "db": {
          "contact_requests": {
            "where": {
              "shortlist_id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "count": 2
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "role_id": "<uuid>",
          "name": "Platform team, Q3 (revised)",
          "status": "open",
          "tentative_result_date": "2026-09-30",
          "entries": [
            {
              "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001",
              "display_name": "Alice Okafor",
              "notified_at": "<timestamp>",
              "contact_status": "pending",
              "email": null
            },
            {
              "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a002",
              "display_name": "Bob Nakamura",
              "notified_at": "<timestamp>",
              "contact_status": "pending",
              "email": null
            },
            {
              "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a003",
              "display_name": "Carol Diaz",
              "notified_at": null,
              "contact_status": null,
              "email": null
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Confirm again. ONE email. Alice and Bob are not re-notified.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/confirm",
        "body": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "status": "open",
          "notified": 1,
          "already_notified": 2,
          "irreversible": true,
          "first_confirmed_at": "<timestamp>",
          "entries": [
            {
              "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a003",
              "display_name": "Carol Diaz",
              "contact_request_id": "<uuid>",
              "notified_at": "<timestamp>"
            }
          ]
        },
        "db": {
          "contact_requests": {
            "where": {
              "shortlist_id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "count": 3
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Carol was inactive when contacted. Accepting refreshes her availability window — answering yes says more than the button she forgot to click.",
      "as": "carol",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/me/contact-requests/{{contact_request_id}}/accept",
        "body": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "status": "accepted",
          "responded_at": "<timestamp>",
          "email_released_at": "<timestamp>",
          "availability_refreshed": true
        },
        "db": {
          "user_availability": {
            "where": {
              "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a003"
            },
            "none_match": {
              "expires_at": null
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/contact-requests"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "requested_by names the colleague who asked, including one who has since left (ADR-0016 §9). A hirer looking at an old approach needs to know who on their side made it before making another.",
        "body": {
          "total": 3,
          "requests": [
            {
              "id": "<uuid>",
              "user": {
                "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001",
                "display_name": "Alice Okafor",
                "github_login": "aliceok"
              },
              "requested_by": {
                "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
                "username": "hank",
                "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
                "active": true
              },
              "status": "pending",
              "email": null,
              "responded_at": null
            },
            {
              "id": "<uuid>",
              "user": {
                "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a002",
                "display_name": "Bob Nakamura",
                "github_login": "bobn"
              },
              "requested_by": {
                "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
                "username": "hank",
                "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
                "active": true
              },
              "status": "pending",
              "email": null,
              "responded_at": null
            },
            {
              "id": "<uuid>",
              "user": {
                "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a003",
                "display_name": "Carol Diaz",
                "github_login": "cdiaz"
              },
              "requested_by": {
                "id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c001",
                "username": "hank",
                "display_name": "Hank Rivera",
                "active": true
              },
              "status": "accepted",
              "email": "carol@example.com",
              "responded_at": "<timestamp>"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/close",
        "body": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "id": "<uuid>",
          "name": "Platform team, Q3 (revised)",
          "status": "closed",
          "entry_count": 3,
          "closed_at": "<timestamp>"
        },
        "db": {
          "shortlists": {
            "where": {
              "id": "{{shortlist}}"
            },
            "all_match": {
              "status": "closed"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A closed round takes no new entries. Staging someone for a finished search would only ever mislead them.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/entries",
        "body": {
          "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a004"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 409,
        "body": {
          "error": "shortlist_closed"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/confirm",
        "body": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 409,
        "body": {
          "error": "shortlist_closed"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists/{{shortlist}}/close",
        "body": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 409,
        "body": {
          "error": "shortlist_closed"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A DRAFT that is never confirmed drops out of the overdue ratio — nothing was promised to anyone.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/shortlists",
        "body": {
          "role_id": "{{acme.role}}",
          "name": "Abandoned idea",
          "tentative_result_date": "2026-08-20"
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "abandoned": "$.id"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "body": {
